# Paths semgrep skips when scripts/semgrep_ci.py scans this repository. A .semgrepignore replaces semgrep's
# built-in list (which would also skip tests/), so it is spelled out here; tests/ is deliberately scanned.
# semgrep already limits a scan to git-tracked files, so .mara-tools/, out/ and other ignored output never
# enter. The seeded review material (fixtures/, calib/samples/) is NOT listed here — semgrep applies this
# file from the git root even when scanning a subdirectory, which would blank the fixture drift check —
# it is excluded per scan through the triage file's `exclude` list instead.
.git/
